WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:02.980
INTRO:
Just a few months ago, the general international

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:06.460
audience had no clue who Volodymyr Zelenskyy
was.

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:12.580
But, ever since Russia invaded Ukraine, Zelenskyy
has transformed into a national hero who’s

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:15.730
willing to stand with his people till the
very last second.

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:19.590
Now, wars aren’t won by any singular person.

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:23.840
Everyone from the military and the civilians
to the donators and the press play significant

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:25.470
roles in securing a victory.

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:29.960
But, with that being said, none of these parties
would be able to contribute to their maximum

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:31.870
ability without great morale.

00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:37.579
And there’s no doubt that Zelenskyy has
done a great job in maintaining spirits high.

00:00:37.579 --> 00:00:41.329
Considering this strong performance, you would
think that Zelenskyy has a lot of experience

00:00:41.329 --> 00:00:45.249
leading teams and people, but this isn’t
actually true.

00:00:45.249 --> 00:00:50.089
In fact, Zelenskyy started off as an entertainer
and he leveraged his popularity to get into

00:00:50.089 --> 00:00:51.089
office.

00:00:51.089 --> 00:00:55.609
While many Ukrainians likely had their doubts
when a former comedian was elected into office,

00:00:55.609 --> 00:00:58.850
Zelenskyy has more than proved that he’s
capable of the role.

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:05.390
So, here’s the story of Volodymyr Zelenskyy
and how he became the savior of Ukraine.

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:10.770
GRITTY BACKGROUND:
Taking a look back, Zelenskyy was born on

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:15.729
January 25, 1978, in the former Ukrainian
Soviet Socialist Republic.

00:01:15.729 --> 00:01:19.890
In terms of heritage, Zelenskyy’s family
was Jewish, and they were severely impacted

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:21.250
by the Holocaust.

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:25.240
Many of them were victims of the Holocaust
and had lost their lives to it.

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:29.200
Meanwhile, Zelenskyy’s grandfather was a
part of the Soviet army and fought against

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:30.200
Germany.

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:34.401
Given this painful past, much of Zelenskyy’s
family and their Jewish friends decided to

00:01:34.401 --> 00:01:39.240
leave the Soviet Union and start fresh lives
in Israel and the United States, but Zelenskyy’s

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:41.070
parents decided to stay.

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:45.780
Zelenskyy’s mother was an engineer while
his father was a math professor, so clearly,

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:49.899
this choice wasn’t based on career limitations
as they would’ve had plenty of opportunities

00:01:49.899 --> 00:01:51.479
abroad as well.

00:01:51.479 --> 00:01:56.240
Anyway, though Zelenskyy was born in modern-day
Ukraine, he spent the first few years of his

00:01:56.240 --> 00:02:00.619
life in the Mongolian city of Erdenet which
is where his father worked at the time.

00:02:00.619 --> 00:02:04.890
It wasn’t until elementary school that Zelenskyy
moved back to Ukraine.

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:08.459
In terms of his school life, his peers say
that the main characteristics they recall

00:02:08.459 --> 00:02:12.709
about Zelenskyy are that he got good grades
and wore an earring.

00:02:12.709 --> 00:02:18.209
Moving into high school, at age 17, Zelenskyy
would join the local KVN team which competed

00:02:18.209 --> 00:02:19.580
in comedy tournaments.

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:24.099
Each team was required to come up with a funny
greeting, improvise some jokes, and compose

00:02:24.099 --> 00:02:27.739
a humorous song that they would perform in
front of the audience and judges.

00:02:27.739 --> 00:02:32.090
Zelenskyy excelled in this competition and
would even be invited to join a legacy team

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:35.980
that would go on to win KVN’s major league
in 1997.

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:40.890
After this victory, Zelenskyy would form his
own comedy team called Kvartal 95 that would

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:45.220
regularly perform at the major leagues between
1998 and 2003.

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:49.020
In the meantime, Zelenskyy also kept up with
school as well.

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:52.940
He passed the English language test at age
16 and would receive an educational grant

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:58.239
to go study in Israel, but Zelenskyy’s father
insisted that he stay in Ukraine.

00:02:58.239 --> 00:03:03.819
So, Zelenskyy would go on to attend Kyiv National
Economic University where he earned his law

00:03:03.819 --> 00:03:04.819
degree.

00:03:04.819 --> 00:03:07.560
Given this traditional education, you would
think that Zelenskyy picked up a corporate

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:10.890
job following college, but this was not the
case.

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:14.750
The comedy competitions that he was doing
on the side had garnered him a decent amount

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:16.959
of popularity within Ukrainian television.

00:03:16.959 --> 00:03:21.409
And, Zelenskyy decided to leverage this popularity
to enter the show business.

00:03:21.409 --> 00:03:27.010
SHOW BUSINESS:
Zelenskyy’s first career within the TV industry

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:31.379
outside comedy was not acting but actually
producing.

00:03:31.379 --> 00:03:36.250
Starting in 2003, Zelenskky began producing
TV shows for a Ukrainian TV channel called

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:37.610
1+1.

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:41.659
The show featured the comedy team that he
founded and given their previous popularity

00:03:41.659 --> 00:03:45.840
with KVN, it didn’t take long for them to
build up a loyal audience.

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:50.610
Around the same time, Zelenskyy also dabbled
with some other TV genres including Ukraine’s

00:03:50.610 --> 00:03:52.790
version of Dancing With The Stars.

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:56.930
This time, he wasn’t a behind-the-scenes
producer or director though, he was actually

00:03:56.930 --> 00:03:59.670
one of the competitors in 2006.

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:04.140
And Zelenskyy would not only become a star
performer on the show, but he would actually

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:05.689
win the entire show.

00:04:05.689 --> 00:04:10.099
As you would guess, this win significantly
rose Zelenskyy’s popularity as he become

00:04:10.099 --> 00:04:11.700
a national TV star.

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:16.110
Zelenskyy would use this newfound popularity
to branch out from comedy and try his hand

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:17.530
at traditional acting.

00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:22.140
In 2008, he would star in his first feature
film called Love in the Big City.

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:26.610
Technically, the move was a romantic comedy,
so Zelenskyy didn’t venture out too far

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:30.880
from his roots, but this was his first time
starring in something much longer than a simple

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:32.830
skit or TV show.

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:39.331
The movie had a rather modest budget of $3.5
million, but it pulled in $9.1 million, so

00:04:39.331 --> 00:04:42.080
it looks like it was a pretty good investment
for the studio.

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:46.770
The studio would go on to fund two sequels
to the movie called Love in the Big City 2

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:48.120
and Love in the Big City 3.

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:53.090
In the first sequel, Zelenskyy remained a
key actor in the film, but in the second sequel,

00:04:53.090 --> 00:04:55.449
he would transition into being a producer.

00:04:55.449 --> 00:04:59.740
Aside from this franchise, Zelenskyy also
worked on the movies Office Romance.

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:05.190
Our Time, Rzhevksy vs. Napoleon, 8 first dates
and its two sequels, and Paddington Bear and

00:05:05.190 --> 00:05:06.420
its sequel.

00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:10.850
With major roles in all of these productions,
Zelenskyy quickly became an A-list celebrity,

00:05:10.850 --> 00:05:15.650
and he would start to use this fame to fight
against what he thought were injustices.

00:05:15.650 --> 00:05:20.669
One example of this was in 2014 when the Ukrainian
Ministry of Culture was attempting to ban

00:05:20.669 --> 00:05:22.510
Russian artists from Ukraine.

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:28.020
Zelenskyy was a staunch proponent against
this legislation and voiced his concerns nationally.

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:33.810
Unfortunately, Ukraine would go on to enact
this ban anyway in 2015, but Zelenskyy did

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:34.810
try.

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:38.600
While these calls went unheard, it wasn’t
long till politicians could no longer ignore

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:41.460
Zelenskyy as he would soon get the people
of Ukraine on his side.

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:48.460
RISE TO POWER:
Politicians often spend decades building up

00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:52.801
major political runs by starting small and
slowly working up the ladder.

00:05:52.801 --> 00:05:57.160
They might start as a representative and then
become a senator and then become a governor

00:05:57.160 --> 00:06:00.240
and then finally, they might run for president.

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:04.170
Even Donald Trump who ran with no political
background had been teasing a presidential

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:06.319
bid as far back as 1988.

00:06:06.319 --> 00:06:14.460
But, for Zelenskyy, his rise to power was
truly something that unfolded overnight.

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:24.139
It all started in 2015 when Zelenskyy starred
in a TV show called Servant of the People.

00:06:24.139 --> 00:06:28.819
In the show, Zelenskyy played a humble schoolteacher
that often ranted about political corruption

00:06:28.819 --> 00:06:31.410
and various shortfalls of the political system.

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:34.780
And many clips from his rants started going
viral on social media.

00:06:34.780 --> 00:06:39.699
Soon enough, a lot of news outlets and journalists
started speculating if Zelenskyy would make

00:06:39.699 --> 00:06:41.140
a political run.

00:06:41.140 --> 00:06:45.500
And all this speculation along with the success
of the show convinced Zelenskyy that he should

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:46.610
give it a shot.

00:06:46.610 --> 00:06:51.560
In March of 2018, the people at Kvartal 95
launched a political party called Servant

00:06:51.560 --> 00:06:52.740
of the People.

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:56.570
Despite the creation of the party, Zelenskyy
didn’t officially announce that he was going

00:06:56.570 --> 00:06:58.330
to run for several months.

00:06:58.330 --> 00:07:02.669
He always gave ambiguous answers similar to
what Trump is doing right now with the 2024

00:07:02.669 --> 00:07:03.669
election.

00:07:03.669 --> 00:07:07.240
Even though Zelenskyy didn’t officially
announce his campaign, a lot of polls included

00:07:07.240 --> 00:07:11.190
him anyway, and he generally performed exceptionally
well.

00:07:11.190 --> 00:07:14.770
It wasn’t till New Year’s Eve of 2018
that Zelenskyy would officially announce his

00:07:14.770 --> 00:07:16.629
campaign on his own show.

00:07:16.629 --> 00:07:21.099
And, once he announced his campaign, he shot
up in the polls from being a favorite to being

00:07:21.099 --> 00:07:22.130
a decisive leader.

00:07:22.130 --> 00:07:26.170
Zelenskyy didn’t campaign like ordinary
politicians though by giving long interviews

00:07:26.170 --> 00:07:27.300
and speeches.

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:31.470
Instead, Zelenskyy went ahead and embraced
what people knew him for comedy.

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:36.090
He posted dozens of humorous videos on YouTube
and Instagram that mocked the political establishment.

00:07:36.090 --> 00:07:40.860
In other words, he cleverly leveraged the
power of social media to run his campaign

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:43.300
which would prove to be extremely effective.

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:48.569
On March 31, 2019, the first round of the
presidential election was completed and Zelenskyy

00:07:48.569 --> 00:07:50.590
would win 30% of the vote.

00:07:50.590 --> 00:07:54.909
For perspective, second place only garnered
16% of the vote.

00:07:54.909 --> 00:08:00.020
And just a few weeks later on April 21, 2019,
the second round of the election would take

00:08:00.020 --> 00:08:04.330
place, and Zelenskyy would win in a landslide
securing 73% of the vote.

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:08.990
So, Zelenskyy hasn’t even been president
for three years yet, but he’s already been

00:08:08.990 --> 00:08:12.820
involved in two of the biggest political controversies
in Ukrainian history.

00:08:12.820 --> 00:08:14.960
Speak about perfect timing.

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:20.139
CONTROVERSY AFTER CONTROVERSY:
With how significant the Russian-Ukrainian

00:08:20.139 --> 00:08:24.729
conflict has become, most of us have completely
forgotten about the Trump-Ukraninan drama

00:08:24.729 --> 00:08:26.639
that unfolded a few years ago.

00:08:26.639 --> 00:08:31.360
But, this was quite a big deal too as it led
to the second impeachment of Donald Trump.

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:36.190
The story goes that shortly after Zelenskyy
was elected, Trump called him and asked him

00:08:36.190 --> 00:08:40.240
to investigate Biden’s business dealing
within Ukraine which seemed reasonable given

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:43.190
that there seemed to be some evidence of potential
corruption.

00:08:43.190 --> 00:08:48.110
The problem though was that Trump used military
aid as a bargaining chip and refused to release

00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:52.380
$391 million worth of aid until Zelenskyy
publicly announced a probe into Biden’s

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:53.610
dealings in Ukraine.

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:57.550
The military aid was supposed to be used to
strengthen Ukraine’s eastern border.

00:08:57.550 --> 00:09:01.750
And today it has become painfully evident
why this was so important.

00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:05.690
Trump ended up releasing the aide after his
phone call with Zelenskyy became public, but

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:08.500
it ended up costing him a second impeachment.

00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:12.700
Just as this fiasco came to an end, Zelenskyy
was hit with another massive hurdle which

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:14.810
was of course the pandemic.

00:09:14.810 --> 00:09:19.270
Handling Covid 19 has been one of the biggest
challenges for politicians around the world.

00:09:19.270 --> 00:09:23.790
From enacting lockdowns and mask mandates
to distributing vaccines and returning to

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:25.080
normal life.

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:29.150
Every step has been heavily scrutinized by
the media and it doesn’t help that people

00:09:29.150 --> 00:09:31.690
are heavily divided on these subjects.

00:09:31.690 --> 00:09:36.210
These issues were no different within Ukraine,
and unfortunately, they’ve experienced four

00:09:36.210 --> 00:09:38.850
major surges since the start of the pandemic.

00:09:38.850 --> 00:09:42.780
You could say that Zelenskyy stood with his
people during the pandemic as well given that

00:09:42.780 --> 00:09:45.910
he caught the illness early on before the
vaccine was approved.

00:09:45.910 --> 00:09:50.080
Nevertheless, like the rest of the world,
Ukraine was just starting to lighten restrictions

00:09:50.080 --> 00:09:53.440
and return to normal life as they moved into
2022.

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:57.021
And then the Russian invasion speculation
started to go through the roof.

00:09:57.021 --> 00:10:01.510
For some reason, It looks like Zelenskyy just
can’t catch a break.

00:10:01.510 --> 00:10:06.810
THE FUTURE OF UKRAINE:
By now, I’m sure all of you guys know what’s

00:10:06.810 --> 00:10:08.620
going on in Ukraine.

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:12.430
After weeks of increasing pressure on Ukraine
by deploying soldiers all around the country,

00:10:12.430 --> 00:10:14.940
Putin decided to invade in the last week of
February.

00:10:14.940 --> 00:10:19.560
At the time of making this video, no country
has really committed to helping Ukraine in

00:10:19.560 --> 00:10:21.140
terms of military aid.

00:10:21.140 --> 00:10:25.770
However, countries and companies around the
world have been working together to financially

00:10:25.770 --> 00:10:27.710
and economically punish Russia.

00:10:27.710 --> 00:10:31.410
This includes loads of sanctions, bans on
Russian aircraft, companies refusing to do

00:10:31.410 --> 00:10:34.840
business with Russia, and tons of pushback
from the public.

00:10:34.840 --> 00:10:39.090
While all of these are valiant efforts in
helping Ukraine, at the end of the day, it’s

00:10:39.090 --> 00:10:43.690
the Ukrainian people that are physically defending
the country, and the helm we have Zelenskyy.

00:10:43.690 --> 00:10:47.660
Right now, it’s unclear how much longer
the conflict will last and what the result

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:48.660
will be.

00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:53.210
There have been a few meetings between representatives
from both countries, but we are yet to receive

00:10:53.210 --> 00:10:54.940
a concrete resolution.

00:10:54.940 --> 00:10:59.060
Looking forward, if Zelenskyy and Ukraine
survive the conflict, there’s no doubt that

00:10:59.060 --> 00:11:03.550
Zelenskyy will be seen as a wartime hero,
and he won’t be leaving the presidential

00:11:03.550 --> 00:11:05.400
position anytime soon.

00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:09.860
Even if things turn sour and Zelenskyy is
captured or worse, he definitely didn’t

00:11:09.860 --> 00:11:14.600
go down without a fight, and I’m sure he’d
be remembered for decades to come.

00:11:14.600 --> 00:11:18.040
For everyone’s sake though, hopefully, we
stick with scenario #1.

00:11:18.040 --> 00:11:19.960
But that’s just what I think.

00:11:19.960 --> 00:11:22.580
Do you guys support Zelenskyy and Ukraine?

00:11:22.580 --> 00:11:23.580
Comment that down below.

00:11:23.580 --> 00:11:28.530
Also, drop a like if you think Zelenskyy is
doing a better job lifelong politicians.

00:11:28.530 --> 00:11:32.800
And of course, consider checking out our international
channels to watch our videos in other languages

00:11:32.800 --> 00:11:42.670
and consider subscribing to see more questions
